  "dom_id": "step-q122565",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Stefany wants to draw a picture using $5$ colors from her $24$-color crayon box. In how many ways can she pick the $5$ colors?",
  "worked_solution": "In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $24$ colors, so $n=24.$ We want to select $5$ of those colors for Stefany to draw her picture, so we have $r=5.$\n\nTherefore, the number of choices is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{24}{C}_{5} & =\\frac{24!}{(24-5)!\\,5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{24!}{19!5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\cdot 23\\cdot 22\\cdot 21\\cdot 20\\cdot \\cancel{19!}}{\\cancel{19!}5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\cdot 23\\cdot 22\\cdot 21\\cdot 20}{5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\,100\\,480}{120} \\\\  & =42\\,504.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
